WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.362
Hi, I'm Lemur!

00:00:02.362 --> 00:00:07.362
ZCode, a coding agent, was reported to build and upload snapshots of local repositories.

00:00:07.362 --> 00:00:11.292
Here's how the fix works, and what the release can prove.

00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:14.549
The fix kept the feature.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:18.226
Checkpoint and restore now live in your own git repository, as a

00:00:18.226 --> 00:00:20.371
hidden ref scoped to the current workspace.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:26.889
As reported, the old workflow archived the workspace and sent it

00:00:26.889 --> 00:00:28.278
to the vendor's storage.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:31.753
A workspace includes dot git: every version of every file.

00:00:32.173 --> 00:00:36.664
The new version writes the snapshot into the repository you already have.

00:00:36.664 --> 00:00:40.782
Git's object store is content-addressed and deduplicated, and it's already there.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:46.437
Point git at a temporary index file, so your real index is never touched.

00:00:46.857 --> 00:00:49.982
Stage everything, but only under the current workspace's path.

00:00:50.402 --> 00:00:53.478
Write that into a tree, and wrap the tree in a commit object.

00:00:53.898 --> 00:00:55.838
Point a hidden ref at it.

00:00:55.838 --> 00:00:58.100
No user-visible branch, and no ordinary commit.

00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:02.814
The open repository answers what the client does now.

00:01:02.814 --> 00:01:08.011
Its notice file lists seventeen outbound-request scenarios, and a snapshot upload isn't one.

00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:10.409
The history isn't there: two commits.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:15.253
Every agent that edits your files needs undo, and undo needs somewhere

00:01:15.253 --> 00:01:16.706
to keep the old state.

00:01:16.706 --> 00:01:18.740
Git already keeps it on your machine.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:24.631
To recap: undo moved into a hidden git ref, built from a

00:01:24.631 --> 00:01:28.695
temporary index, and the open repository shows the present, not the past.

00:01:29.115 --> 00:01:31.182
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:31.182 --> 00:01:31.772
I'm Lemur.

00:01:31.772 --> 00:01:32.068
Bye!
